          "path": "_m/w/s/0/e/sun-yat-sen-memorial-hall-guangzhou-wp/canton-1996-303.jpg",
          "filename": "Canton 1996 303.jpg",
          "caption": "Sun Yat Sen Memoria. Guangzhou, China\nThis memorial building (1931) was erected, a few years after his death, on the very spot where Dr. Sun Yat Sen set up his revolutionary headquarters in 1923. A co-founder of the Kuomintang Party, he made a United Front with Stalin, and is therefore revered (and his legacy claimed) by both the CCP and the KMT. He died in 1925, long before the post-WWII struggle between the two parties would have forced him to make a decision.",
          "alt": "Sun Yat Sen Memoria. Guangzhou, China\nThis memorial building (1931) was erected, a few years after his death, on the very spot where Dr. Sun Yat Sen set up his revolutionary headquarters in 1923. A co-founder of the Kuomintang Party, he made a United Front with Stalin, and is therefore revered (and his legacy claimed) by both the CCP and the KMT. He died in 1925, long before the post-WWII struggle between the two parties would have forced him to make a decision.",
          "width": 1693,
          "height": 1133,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
